A. Check external libraries required to build full functionality of TexMol
(these libraries will be found by cmake if you have ones installed)

1. Boost (1.41.0 has been tested) - required for basic build
2. GSL (1.15 has been tested)     - required for coarse grain library
3. HDF5 (1.8.5 has been tested)   - required for heirarchical volume handling in VolMagick
4. CGAL (4.0 has been tested)     - required for pockettunnel, secondary structure elucidation
5. FFTW (3.2.4 has been tested)   - required for volutils and multi-resolution surface
6. NFFT (3.1.3 has been tested)   - required for generalized Born energy, coarse grain library, multi-resolution surface
7. PETSC (3.2-p7 has been tested) - required for Poisson Bolzmann energy and potential
8. LAPACK & BLAS                  - required for secondary structure elucidation, pokect tunnel, interface stats, and molsurf

*** You can download those libraries here **

   http://cvcweb.ices.utexas.edu/3rdparty

***

--->
B. Build

To build:
$ cd $BUILD_DIR
$ cmake $SOURCE_DIR
$ make

BUILD_DIR - a location to place files generated during the build.
            It can be the same as the SOURCE_DIR
SOURCE_DIR - The location of the project's root CMakeLists.txt file.


Once you've built the project, the binary will be in bin/ and any libraries
created during the process will be in lib/.


To buid PB, you must set certain environment variables to 
find the PETSc libraries.  Here are the variables I have been
setting in my .bashrc file:

PETSC_DIR=/net/axon/workspace/arand/petsc-3.1-p5
PETSC_ARCH=linux-gnu-c-debug
